    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (1 test class; the other two files are the abstract base and an audit-log support helper).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds **idempotent create** support to `POST /api/owners` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`.\n\n**How it works:**\n- A new `currentIdempotencyKey()` helper reads the `Idempotency-Key` request header via `RequestContextHolder`. I read it from the ambient request rather than adding a method parameter so the OpenAPI-generated `OwnersApi.addOwner` contract stays unchanged (the `@Override` signature is untouched).\n- A `ConcurrentHashMap<String, Integer>` (`idempotentCreates`) maps each seen key to the id of the owner originally created under it.\n- In `addOwner`:\n  - If the key is present and already recorded, the original owner is re-fetched and returned with **200 OK** (via the existing `buildOwnerDto`), skipping the create pipeline \u2014 so it no longer trips the duplicate-identity `409`.\n  - Otherwise the normal `createOwner` pipeline runs, and **only on a successful `201 CREATED`** is the key\u2192id recorded.\n\nThis satisfies the acceptance test `coreIdempotentRepeat`: first create returns 2xx, the identical repeat with the same key returns 200 with the same id. Keys are only recorded on success, and absent/blank headers fall through to normal behavior, so all other create rules (validation, quotas, duplicate detection, auditing) are unaffected.",
