    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered sequence of validations and side-effects for `POST /api/owners`, from request arrival to response.\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Before the controller method runs (framework-level)\n\n1. **Authorization gate** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller lacking the `OWNER_ADMIN` role \u2192 **403** (via Spring Security / `ExceptionControllerAdvice`).\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** \u2014 `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`. All JSR-380 constraints run here; any failure \u2192 **400** (`MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 `handleMethodArgumentNotValidException`). Constraints:\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Size(max=10)`\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(...\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@Pattern((?s).*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `addressLine1` \u2014 `@Pattern((?s).*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max=255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern((?s).*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max=255)`, `@Email`\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 `addOwner()` idempotency short-circuit\n\n3. **Idempotency-Key lookup** \u2014 if the `Idempotency-Key` header matches a prior create, returns the existing owner as **200 OK** (no new side-effect).\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 `createOwner()` pipeline (in this exact order)\n\n4. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`).\n5. **`normalizeAndValidateFields`** \u2014 mutations + validations; any failure \u2192 **400**:\n   - **Normalizes address**: composes flat `address` from `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`, upper-cases, expands `ST`/`RD`/`AVE` abbreviations.\n   - **Normalizes email**: lower-cases and trims; then validates against `EMAIL_PATTERN` and rejects disposable-email domains (`DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` blocklist).\n   - **Postcode-for-city consistency check** (`isPostcodeValidForCity`).\n   - **Normalizes telephone** to E.164 form, with a national-length check.\n6. **Future-date check** \u2014 supplied `registrationDate` after today \u2192 **400**.\n7. **Resolve registration date** (`resolveRegistrationDate` \u2192 `toBusinessDay`) \u2014 rolls a missing/weekend/public-holiday date forward to the next business day; **mutates** `owner.registrationDate`.\n8. **Per-day cap** \u2014 if \u2265100 owners already registered on that resolved date \u2192 **429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS**.\n9. **Set `householdId`** (SHA-256 derived) and **set `identityKey`** on the owner.\n10. **Duplicate-identity gate** (`isDuplicate` by identity key) \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**.\n11. **Existing-household gate** \u2014 if `sharesHousehold` is not true and the household already exists (`hasExistingHousehold`) \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**.\n12. **Per-city cap** \u2014 if \u226550 owners already in that city \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**.\n13. **`assignRegistrationAttributes`** \u2014 sets derived fields: `customerCode` (SHA-256 hash + collision-dedup suffix), `membershipNumber`, `householdId` (again), `namesakeCount`, `householdMemberCount`, and possible-duplicate flags (`possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`).\n14. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (`@Transactional`). At the Hibernate flush, **entity-level Bean Validation** runs on `Owner`/`Person`: `firstName`/`lastName` `@NotEmpty`, `address` `@NotEmpty`, `city` `@NotEmpty`, `postcode` `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`, `telephone` `@NotEmpty` + `@Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)`. `pets` cascade is `ALL` but no pets are attached on this path. A DB integrity violation \u2192 **404** (`handleDataIntegrityViolationException`).\n15. **Audit log** \u2014 writes to the dedicated `AUDIT` logger (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber).\n16. **Record idempotency mapping** \u2014 back in `addOwner`, stores `Idempotency-Key \u2192 new id` (on 201 with a body id).\n17. **Build response** \u2014 sets `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, builds `OwnerDto` (which also computes the per-response `bulkSignupWarning` flag), returns **201 CREATED**.\n\n## Notes on what does *not* apply\n\n- **No `@Transactional` around the whole pipeline** \u2014 only `saveOwner` (write) and the read helpers each run in their own transaction, so the many `findAllOwners()`-based checks (duplicate, household, namesake, per-city, per-day counts) are non-atomic with the final save.\n- **No `@InitBinder`/`WebDataBinder`, no validation groups, no custom `ConstraintValidator` on the owner path** (`PetAgeValidator` applies only to pets).\n- **No `@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist`/`@EntityListeners`** on `Owner`, `Person`, or `BaseEntity` \u2014 every default/derived value is set explicitly in the controller, not via JPA lifecycle callbacks.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: the entity-level `postcode`/`telephone` patterns and `@NotEmpty` constraints (step 14) partly duplicate DTO-level checks, and the per-day/per-city/duplicate gates (steps 8, 11, 12) read via separate read-only transactions before a non-transactional save, so they are racy under concurrent creation. I've only described the code as it stands and changed nothing."
